{"type": "tool_call", "n": 13, "ts": 1790153629.919445, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MEMO \u2014 US (Halvard Systems Inc., USD) March 2026 Revenue by Stream\nPrepared 2026-04-03 for the CFO. Read-only analysis; no journal entries posted, reversed, matched or flagged \u2014 books unchanged.\n\nSUMMARY (period activity, March 2026, per general ledger)\n  Subscription Revenue (4000)            USD 52,300.00\n  Usage Revenue (4100)                   USD    977.00\n  Professional Services Revenue (4200)   USD  7,500.00\n  ---------------------------------------------------\n  TOTAL US MARCH REVENUE                 USD 60,777.00\n\nEach stream total agrees exactly to get_account_balance period activity for 2026-03 (4000: -52,300.00; 4100: -977.00; 4200: -7,500.00 in debit-minus-credit terms) and to the sum of the individual ledger entries below. All 8 entries are status=posted, source=ar, and carry attached support.\n\nTRAIL \u2014 SUBSCRIPTION REVENUE (4000) = 52,300.00\n  JE-00222  2026-03-01  INV-2111  Acme Logistics   Subscription Mar-26   +18,000.00\n  JE-00224  2026-03-01  INV-2113  Corvid Retail    Subscription Mar-26   +11,500.00\n  JE-00219  2026-03-01  INV-2115  Fairview Labs    Subscription Mar-26    +9,400.00\n  JE-00215  2026-03-01  INV-2112  Beacon Health    Subscription Mar-26    +8,000.00\n  JE-00225  2026-03-01  INV-2114  Evergreen Bank   Subscription Mar-26    +6,200.00\n  JE-00275  2026-03-20  CM-0031   Beacon Health    SLA credit (Feb incident) -800.00  [support DOC-0192; credit memo explicitly states it reduces subscription revenue]\n  Gross invoiced 53,100.00 less credit memo 800.00 = 52,300.00\n  (Every entry: Dr 1100 A/R / Cr 4000, credit memo reversed.)\n\nTRAIL \u2014 USAGE REVENUE (4100) = 977.00\n  JE-00236  2026-03-04  INV-2180  Acme Logistics   API usage overage \u2013 February 2026 (billed in arrears)   +977.00  [support DOC-0164]\n\nTRAIL \u2014 PROFESSIONAL SERVICES REVENUE (4200) = 7,500.00\n  JE-00255  2026-03-10  INV-2118  Fairview Labs    Implementation services \u2013 March 2026   +7,500.00\n\nSCOPE NOTES\n  - \"Revenue\" here = the three operating streams requested. Excluded: 4800 Intercompany Management Fee Income and 4900 Interest Income.\n  - No Deferred Revenue (2200) releases and no Unbilled Receivable (1300) accruals hit these accounts in March; all March revenue is invoice-driven.\n\nOBSERVATION FOR CONTROLLER (no action taken, per instruction not to change the books)\n  - Usage cut-off: the only usage revenue in March (JE-00236, 977.00) is for FEBRUARY consumption, billed in arrears per invoice DOC-0164. There is no March-usage accrual in 1300 Unbilled Receivables for the period (zero activity). If Acme (or other customers) incurred overage in March, March usage revenue is understated and February is likewise recognized a month late. This is a consistent-lag pattern rather than an error in the ledger totals, but the CFO should read the 977.00 as \"February usage recognized in March.\" Recommend the controller decide whether a March usage accrual is required before close.\n  - The 800.00 Beacon Health SLA credit relates to a February incident but was issued 2026-03-20 and correctly reduces March subscription revenue as a credit memo; noted only so the CFO understands why Beacon's March net is 7,200.00 vs. its 8,000.00 invoice.\n"}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
